<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- Static RRO that adds com.google.android.webview to the Android 9 WebView provider list
     WITHOUT modifying or re-signing framework-res.apk.

     The requirements below are the ones verified from the AOSP 9 sources cached in refs/aosp9/
     (tag android-9.0.0_r35, hashes in reports/AOSP9_SOURCE_PROVENANCE.md):
       * must live in /vendor/overlay or /product/overlay: PackageManagerService.java:2606-2620 scans
         those two directories with PARSE_IS_SYSTEM_DIR | SCAN_AS_SYSTEM.
       * NO signing requirement for such a file: the "must be signed with the platform certificate"
         throw at PackageManagerService.java:11232-11249 is inside the ELSE branch of the
         (scanFlags & SCAN_AS_SYSTEM) test, so it applies only to overlays that are not on a system
         partition.
       * <overlay> needs targetPackage (non-null), an EXPLICIT isStatic="true" (PackageParser
         defaults it to false) and priority 0..9999: PackageParser.java:2055-2094.
       * matching is by TYPE NAME + ENTRY KEY NAME, not numeric id, and <overlayable>/<public> are
         not enforced on 9 (Omap is Android 10+). Production proof: /vendor/overlay/
         FrameworksResCommon.apk on a shipping Android 9 arm64 device overrides 36 NON-PUBLIC
         android entries, and /vendor/overlay/CarrierConfigResCommon.apk overrides a file-type xml
         resource the same way this one does.
       * PMS then asks installd for the idmap (PackageManagerService.java:832-834); a failure there is
         caught, logged as "Failed to generate idmap for ..." (:839-841) and the overlay is skipped -
         silent, not a boot loop.
       * static overlays cannot be upgraded: to change this file, replace the APK AND delete
         /data/resource-cache, then reboot.
     Native side, verified from frameworks/native cmds/idmap/scan.cpp (android-9.0.0_r35):
       * scan.cpp:179-182 - `if (is_static_overlay) return priority; return NO_OVERLAY_TAG;` so a
         NON-static overlay in this directory is never mapped at boot. Hence isStatic="true".
       * scan.cpp:118-120 - priority outside 0..9999 returns -1; :123-126 reads isStatic from the
         attribute's Res_value.data != 0; :148-151 requires the target string to match exactly.
       * scan.cpp:140-146 - requiredSystemPropertyName/Value, when present, can silently skip the
         overlay; this manifest emits neither, so nothing can gate it off.
       * scan.cpp contains NO signature or certificate code at all (grep: zero matches), which is the
         second, independent confirmation that a /vendor/overlay RRO is not signature-checked.
     create.cpp could NOT be retrieved (the fetch returned binary junk and was deleted), so no claim
     here rests on it.

     This source tree is the aapt2 input. The deployed artefact is generated by
     tools/build_overlay.py, which writes the same content as verified AXML + resources.arsc
     without aapt; see reports/INTEGRATION_PLAN.md.
-->
<manifest xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    package="com.qoder.webviewprovider.overlay"
    android:versionCode="1"
    android:versionName="1">
    <application android:hasCode="false" android:label="WebView Provider Overlay" />
    <overlay
        android:targetPackage="android"
        android:isStatic="true"
        android:priority="10" />
</manifest>
